1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,900
Some days, the hardest part isn't finding an answer.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:07,700
It's explaining what we really feel.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,000
This is Sela. Nadia, a fictional adult, starts to write.

4
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:18,033
Replies here come from a labelled test program, not from Meta.

5
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:21,700
Sela notices what she meant: an interpretation, not a fact.

6
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:27,667
A meaning check compares it with her words. Nadia decides.

7
00:00:30,467 --> 00:00:34,267
But what if a wrong interpretation was already saved?

8
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:39,500
This is a scripted test mistake: "sometimes" became "always".

9
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:43,200
The meaning check flags it as an important change.

10
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:48,733
Nadia fixes it in her own words.

11
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,300
Before saving, Sela shows everything this will affect.

12
00:00:57,867 --> 00:01:01,667
One correction reaches everything that depends on it.

13
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:07,600
The Meaning Integrity Engine traces summaries, links and requests in one step.

14
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,700
The old summary needs review again.

15
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:15,533
Its share link is stopped.

16
00:01:16,267 --> 00:01:22,667
The request to the simulated service is cancelled. What others already read can't be recalled.

17
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:27,467
"My story over time" shows Nadia's notes across the days.

18
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:32,967
Her own words, with source versions. No AI, no scores, no diagnosis.

19
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:36,767
She picks two notes to bring to a summary.

20
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:43,000
If she wants, Nadia picks one small step.

21
00:01:44,367 --> 00:01:47,967
She writes it herself: two questions for a consultation.

22
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:53,967
No reminders, no day counts. She can skip it.

23
00:01:54,167 --> 00:01:55,967
Next, a sheet to bring along.

24
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:00,800
Sela says it clearly: not a medical passport, record or diagnosis.

25
00:02:02,767 --> 00:02:06,767
Each statement points to an original quote and its source version.

26
00:02:08,333 --> 00:02:12,333
This preview is exactly what a recipient would receive.

27
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:18,600
Nadia approves this exact version. Only approved versions can be shared.

28
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:24,467
When she's ready, Nadia can send the sheet to a service.

29
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:30,333
Here the recipient is a simulated service, not a real clinic or practitioner.

30
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:34,867
The service proposes times. Nadia chooses.

31
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:39,667
No real appointment is made in this demo.

32
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,100
Nadia can revoke access at any time.

33
00:02:46,067 --> 00:02:49,967
Future access is blocked. Copies already viewed can't be recalled.

34
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:54,500
AI should help us explain our story, not take over its meaning.

35
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:58,100
Your story. Your meaning. Your next step.

36
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,900
Sela. Beyond being heard.
